y","label":"text","orig":"Initial value","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":672.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":333.3333333333333,"r":372.6666666666667,"t":681.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,13],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/56","text":"Initial value"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"=1","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":673.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":402.3333333333333,"r":414.3333333333333,"t":679.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/57","text":"=1"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"t = 20","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":672.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":508.0,"r":530.6666666666666,"t":680.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,6],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/58","text":"t = 20"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"1.0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":666.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":540.6666666666666,"r":552.0,"t":674.0},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/59","text":"1.0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"0.0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":652.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":540.6666666666666,"r":552.0,"t":660.0},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/60","text":"0.0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"1.0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":620.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":542.3333333333334,"r":551.6666666666666,"t":627.0},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/61","text":"1.0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"1","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":587.3333333333334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":377.3333333333333,"r":386.0,"t":632.0},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/62","text":"1"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"0.0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":606.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":541.3333333333334,"r":552.0,"t":614.0},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/63","text":"0.0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"10 15 20","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":586.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":348.0,"r":377.3333333333333,"t":594.0},"charspan":[0,8],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/64","text":"10 15 20"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"X","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":585.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":440.33333333333337,"r":452.33333333333337,"t":591.0},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/65","text":"X"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"X","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":584.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":478.0,"r":493.33333333333337,"t":591.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/66","text":"X"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Finally, we consider a 2 -d NS system for a viscous, incompressible fluid in vorticity form, which reads","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":335.9647743929205,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":319.5000000000001,"r":558.0048747999999,"t":355.7944558000002},"charspan":[0,104],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/67","text":"Finally, we consider a 2 -d NS system for a viscous, incompressible fluid in vorticity form, which reads"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"s t = γ x s y -γ y s x + ν ∆ s + u ( x, y, t ) , ∆ γ = -s, ( x, y ) ∈ [0 , 2] 2 , t ∈ [0 , 20] , (9)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":297.45788987723364,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":331.5140000000001,"r":558.0003916000002,"t":322.0444558000002},"charspan":[0,100],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/68","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"where γ represents the stream function, ∆ is the Laplacian operator, and ν = 0 . 001 . Additionally, u ( x, y, t ) = u 3 ( t ) ×{ 0 . 1 sin[2 π ( x + y )] + cos[2 π ( x + y )] } is the forcing function, where u 3 ( t ) is a function obtained from a GRF. The system is defined over a square domain with dimensions [0 , 2] 2 , and the time interval is [0 , 20] . Under this condition, we can express the stream function as the vorticity, i.e., γ = -∆ -1 s . In the discrete scenario within the Fourier domain, this corresponds to ˜ γ = -1 / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s . To facilitate the training, we augment the first layer of SymNet with i k / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s and i l / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s in the Fourier domain. Then after training, Figure 5 demonstrates that our framework achieves the accurate operator learning in modeling the underlying dynamics, enabling the precise and stable prediction of system evolutions, even the initial values and parameter functions outside the training set distribution. Additional training details and experimental results for the above parametric PDE systems are provided in Appendix B.4.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":87.93377439292044,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":319.5000000000002,"r":558.0049278000001,"t":283.1064558000002},"charspan":[0,1111],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/69","text":"where γ represents the stream function, ∆ is the Laplacian operator, and ν = 0 . 001 . Additionally, u ( x, y, t ) = u 3 ( t ) ×{ 0 . 1 sin[2 π ( x + y )] + cos[2 π ( x + y )] } is the forcing function, where u 3 ( t ) is a function obtained from a GRF. The system is defined over a square domain with dimensions [0 , 2] 2 , and the time interval is [0 , 20] . Under this condition, we can express the stream function as the vorticity, i.e., γ = -∆ -1 s . In the discrete scenario within the Fourier domain, this corresponds to ˜ γ = -1 / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s . To facilitate the training, we augment the first layer of SymNet with i k / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s and i l / ( k 2 + l 2 )˜ s in the Fourier domain. Then after training, Figure 5 demonstrates that our framework achieves the accurate operator learning in modeling the underlying dynamics, enabling the precise and stable prediction of system evolutions, even the initial values and parameter functions outside the training set distribution. Additional training details and experimental results for the above parametric PDE systems are provided in Appendix B.4."}],"version":"1.10.0"}